s  as soon as you have no godwin and now  you have no mike evans you're already  without antonio brown now there's no  lender for that i mean they basically  didn't have a chance at that point and  brady's out there with a bunch of guys  who  probably more than anything he's played  with lesser receivers over his career we  talked about that on sunday but just to  have the reps in the chemistry with  these guys he wasted all those reps on  the guys who were out of the game and  hurt but i mean for them to lose a game  at home where all they have to do is  score more than nine i mean tom brady  hasn't been shut out in 15 years and i  think the reason is and give dennis  allen a ton of credit just because he's  done it over and over again but  not not very many defenses can rush the  passer across the board with davenport  with tuttle with david onyamata with cam  jordan who missed the prior week so i  had fresh legs coming back and he looked  fresh the way he was flying around that  football field but they also have five  great cover guys to have the combination  of the rush and the cover players i  can't think of another defense that is  as dominant on both ends of the spectrum  that's just a hard combination to find  and brady took it right on the chin  and you forgot about mentioning  linebackers demario davis is a top five  middle linebacker he is absolutely  fantastic we talked about him he can hit  he can tackle he can cover he can blitz  he can do it all and kwon alexander like  quan alexander he was a first round  draft choice and he didn't work out for  san francisco and he kind of bounced  around but it seems like he's found a  home you know in new orleans he he looks  like his old self like athletic fast  making plays celebrating so he's brought  him a lot of energy and a lot of juice  as well  that's a great point cause i remember  kwon alexander covered gronk and how  many times you see gronk run that route  he runs it right to the linebacker and  he turns around and breaks right back to  the sideline and when he tried to break  back the silence kwon was all over him  he was running to the sideline before  gronk even decided that he was going to  go that direction so you got to give  credit to all these guys and demario  davis man even when i was watching the  week eight game demario davis was going  screen to the right the whole defense  was running to the right before the play  so yes he has all the physical tools but  probably more than anything his mental  and leadership stuff that just lining up  the defensive backs talking and lining  up the defensive front he appears to me  to be the leader of that entire defense  and you see what what they're producing  imagine if the saints had a quarterback  man if it weren't taysom hill we'd be  talking about a potential super bowl  team here  brother i was just sitting here thinking  the same thing i'm like how frustrating  is it to have a top defense and i've  been there we had the worst offense in  the league and the number one defense in  the nfl when i was with the chargers  back in 1998 i think it was it's very  frustrating but defensively you have to  change your mindset and you completely  say we're going to forget about the  offense we're going to try to score  points we're going to get turnovers  we're going to give them field position  we're going to do whatever we have to do  to make sure we make their life easier  we can't depend on them to win the  football game we have to win a football  game and that's just a change of mindset  that's right and nobody wants to talk  about it but antonio brown now becomes  one of the most important pieces on  tampa and one of the most important  pieces coming back in the whole nfl  because if they didn't have him they  would be in a world of trouble who knows  how long mike evans gonna miss with the  hammy they have to have another wide  receiver on the outside probably scotty  miller before mike evans gets back it's  scot